course: dictionary
lesson: 10654
title: The universe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The universe is everything that exists: all of space, time, matter and energy, including all the stars, planets and galaxies. «The universe is expanding, which means it is getting bigger over time.» Swap in your meaning: the whole of everything is getting bigger over time. That makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Context clues help you see how big the word is. «Scientists do not know whether the universe has an edge or goes on forever; many think it has no edge.» Words like edge and forever show that the universe means all of space, not just one room, one town or one planet.
explain: The word has a second meaning. A universe can be a whole world of its own, like the imaginary world of a story or film, as in «the Marvel universe». Read the words around it to decide which meaning the writer means: space itself, or an imagined world.
fact: The universe is everything that exists, including all space, time, matter and energy.
fact: The Earth is one planet orbiting the Sun, the Sun is one star in the Milky Way galaxy, and the Milky Way is one of billions of galaxies in the universe.
fact: Scientists think the universe began with the Big Bang about 13.8 billion years ago, and it is still expanding.
fact: «Expanding» means getting bigger over time.
fact: A universe can also mean an imagined world, like «the Marvel universe», which means the world of those stories and films.
exercise: «The universe is expanding, which means it is getting bigger over time.» What does expanding mean? | Turning into a star | Standing still for ever | *Getting bigger over time | Getting smaller and darker
exercise: In a film, «the Marvel universe» means what? | A kind of telescope | The Sun and nothing else | The planet Earth and its Moon | *An imagined world of its own, like in a story or film
exercise: «Scientists do not know whether the universe has an edge or goes on forever.» Which meaning of universe fits here? | A school library | A small room in a house | A single star | *Everything that exists, all of space
test: Which of these is part of the universe? | Your bedroom | A pencil case | *The Milky Way galaxy | Your school bag
test: «The night sky is dark although there are countless stars, because the universe had a beginning.» Why is the night sky dark? | *Light from very distant stars has not had time to reach us | Clouds cover every star | Stars only shine in the day | The Sun is switched off at night
exam: Which use of universe means an imagined world? | The edge of the universe | *the Marvel universe, with its heroes and villains | The Milky Way in the universe | The universe is expanding
